          "Catholic intellectual life at its best repeats this conversion without despising the path. The Church Fathers baptize philosophy; they do not burn the libraries. Justin’s martyrdom shows that the disciple of the Logos may still die at the empire’s hands—thought is not a bargain for safety.",
