          "Cyprian teaches that the episcopate is one—each bishop holds the whole in solidary unity with the college. The bishop is not a isolated franchise owner; he is a sharer in one episcopate. Catholic doctrine of collegiality and of the unity of the episcopal college finds an early Latin articulation here, later developed at Vatican II without abandoning the primacy Cyprian also honored in his way.",
