          "Ambrose teaches the newly baptized that the sacramental signs reveal realities exceeding what the senses perceive. What the eye sees is water; what faith receives is burial and resurrection with Christ. What the tongue tastes is bread and wine; what the soul receives is the Body and Blood of the Lord. Catholic sacramental realism in the Latin West drinks from this mystagogical spring. The signs are not pure symbols of absent things; they are the instruments of present grace under Christ’s institution.",
