          "This boundary protects both sides of the mystery. Without real participation, salvation is external and legal only. Without the denial of essential identity, salvation becomes pantheism and the Creator-creature distinction collapses.",
          "Theosis is therefore Christological and pneumatological: we share in God because the Word took flesh and because the Spirit communicates the life of God. It is not a technique of self-divinization.",
          "Western scholastic talk of the light of glory and the beatific vision, and Eastern hesychast talk of uncreated light, operate in different idioms around this same boundary. Maximus is a common father for both when read carefully.",
