          "This doctrine has pastoral importance. Souls afraid of losing themselves in God can be shown John’s end: the self is found, not destroyed. Souls tempted to a spirituality of pure self-erasure can be corrected by the same end. The creature remains a creature; the creature becomes a creature fully alive with God’s life.",
