          "The principle anticipates and joins the Tridentine emphasis on seminaries and formation. Thomas’s Augustinian seriousness about the ordered life of the minister shows in the episcopal demand that the clergy be capable of the office’s spiritual and doctrinal weight. Formation is not pure academic credential; it is the shaping of men who will not become wounds.",
          "Form clergy as mercy to the people. Prefer Thomas’s ranking to pure ordination without formation as a solution to scarcity. Let the flock’s health still measure the standards of the men placed at the altar.",
