          "Christian community can transform the desert from solitary struggle into shared discipleship under a common rule. Pachomius’s permanent gift is this koinonia—the father of cenobites’ discovery that the desert’s fire can be lived together, under a rule that outlasts the first generation’s enthusiasm."
