          "The homilies describe the difficulty of learning this breath—distraction, dryness, the residual resistance of the old man. The difficulty is not a reason to stop; it is the ordinary path of a soul being taught to live from the center. Macarius’s imagery is physiological and mystical together: the heart as the organ of the new life’s respiration under God.",
