          "Fellow prisoners’ testimony records Brandsma’s gentleness and fidelity under the extreme. The Carmelite’s interior life and the priest’s exterior care meet in a place designed to destroy both. The regime’s intent is the reduction of the person to pure material; the priest’s intent is the continued service of the person under God until the end. The office remains when every institutional support is removed.",
          "Hold the priest’s office as remaining under every condition. Prefer Brandsma’s camp pastoral care to pure despair that the vocation ends when the structures end. Let the souls within reach still define the ministry under the Cross.",
          "When structures collapse, prefer the care of the nearest souls to pure paralysis. Prefer the martyr’s final parish to every identity that only knows the institution. The office remains; the camp remains a place where it can still be exercised under grace.",
