          "Reform of the Church after Trent requires a pope who will apply the decrees to Rome itself—not only to distant dioceses. Pius V’s permanent gift is this applied reform—the Dominican’s proof that the center can live the council, and that only then does the council become the whole Church’s conversion rather than a distant code."
