          "The liturgy is a common good of the Latin Church: unity of rite serves unity of faith in a fractured age. Pius V’s permanent gift is this standardization under pressure—the Dominican pope’s proof that a shared missal can be a form of charity for a Church that must pray as one if she is to believe as one."
