          "The Jesuit formation orders both—Mass, the Office’s Marian dimension, the Exercises’ Christocentric and Marian affections—into the same pedagogy that formed Faber and Aloysius. Stanislaus receives the ordinary and makes it the strength of an extraordinary early fidelity. The fuel is available to every young person under the Church’s ordinary life; the saint is the one who burned it for a complete gift.",
