          "Papal responsibility for the whole Church includes the duty to correct and, when required, to confront. Gregory VII’s permanent gift is this costly responsibility—the reforming pope’s proof that the keys include the burden of a judgment that princes may refuse, and that the refusal does not cancel the duty."
