          "The decretals and the conciliar canons address the concrete corruption of the age: the buying of offices, the neglect of the pastoral cure, the violence of the powerful against the weak. Law’s severity is ordered to the protection of the holy and the small. The same pope who claimed high jurisdiction used it to legislate for the integrity of the Eucharist and the relief of the destitute.",
