          "Pius XII’s Mystici Corporis Christi presents the Church as the Mystical Body of Christ—Christ and the members as one complex reality of grace, not a pure association of individuals under a shared label. Catholic ecclesiology’s modern classical expression finds a major charter here. The encyclical orders the visible society and the invisible communion of grace under the same Head. The Holy Spirit is the soul of the Body. Membership, the sacraments, and the hierarchy are situated within a living organism of charity, not within a pure juridical machine.",
