          "His travel to the Holy Land, to India, to the United Nations, and beyond enacted a new style of papacy: present on the world stage, speaking of peace and human dignity, still visibly the successor of Peter. Presence ad extra requires identity ad intra. A Church that only conserves itself stagnates; a Church that only adapts forgets why she went out. Paul VI’s effort was to hold both movements in one mission.",
