          "The Jesus of Nazareth books enact the same conviction: the only adequate response to the crisis of the figure of Jesus in modern culture is a renewed, rigorous, believing attention to who he is in the Gospels and the Church’s faith. Benedict writes as a theologian who can pray and as a pastor who can think. The Person is not a projection of the community; the community exists because of the Person.",
