          "Synodality is a way of walking together under the bishops and the pope—not a parliament that replaces the magisterium. Francis’s permanent ecclesiological gift is this ordered walking—the emphasis that forces the Church to listen without ceasing to be the Church that teaches, under a constitution that has always known both the shepherds’ charge and the flock’s voice in the discernment of the path."
