          "Montfort calls Mary the mold of God—to be formed in her is to be formed in the likeness of Jesus. Catholic Marian theology finds in this image a compact statement of maternal mediation in the order of formation. God the Son took flesh in her; the members of the Son are formed after the same pattern under her care. When formation is treated as pure self-fashioning, Montfort’s mold corrects it. When Mary is treated as pure external helper without formative role, the same image corrects that too.",
          "The mold is not a pure rival artisan; it is the chosen instrument of the Artisan. Montfort’s confidence in Marian formation rests on the Incarnation’s fact: the path God chose to give us Jesus is the path he continues to use to form Jesus in us. The Secret of Mary compresses this pedagogy for souls ready to enter it.",
          "Seek formation in Mary’s mold for the likeness of Jesus. Prefer Montfort’s image to pure self-made spirituality. Let the Mother still form the members of the Son under the same economy of the Incarnation.",
          "When the spiritual life lacks a formative principle, prefer the French school’s Marian mold. Prefer being shaped to every spirituality that only knows pure self-construction. The likeness of Jesus remains the end under the Mother’s care.",
          "Mary is the mold of God: to be formed in her is to be formed in the likeness of Jesus. Montfort’s permanent formative gift is this mold—the missionary’s proof that the Incarnation’s path is still the Church’s path of sanctification, under a Mother who exists to reproduce the Son’s features in those who entrust themselves to her."
