          "His own life—abandoned by some superiors, walking poor roads, preaching under fatigue—embodies the doctrine. The Letter to the Friends of the Cross trains a community of those who will not negotiate away the Cross for pure ease. The Marian consecration does not cancel this; it strengthens the soul for it under the Mother of the crucified.",
          "Expect the Cross as portion of Wisdom’s friends. Prefer Montfort’s normalcy of opposition to pure triumphal mission as the only model. Let poverty and resistance still be interpretable as the path under the same Wisdom who was crucified.",
          "When mission meets resistance, prefer the French missionary’s ranking. Prefer the Friends of the Cross to every spirituality that only knows pure results without the Cross. The portion remains; the Wisdom remains the crucified and risen Lord under God.",
          "The Cross is the portion of those who love Eternal Wisdom: missionary poverty and opposition are normal. Montfort’s permanent missionary gift is this expected Cross—the poor priest’s proof that the love of Christ includes the share of his sufferings, under a consecration to Mary that prepares the soul to carry it without surprise."
