          "The divine motherhood orders the other Marian privileges in Scheeben’s vision. Immaculate conception, holiness, and mediation are intelligible as consequences and participations under the unique relation of the Mother of God. The supernatural organism has a created summit under the uncreated Word—and that summit is maternal.",
          "Rank the divine motherhood at the peak of created grace under Christ. Prefer Scheeben’s dogmatic Mariology to pure peripheral devotion. Let the Mother of God still stand as the highest created realization of the order grace establishes under the Son.",
          "When Mariology is marginalized or exaggerated, prefer the Cologne theologian’s placement. Prefer the supernatural organism’s summit to every spirituality that only knows pure optional Mary or pure independence from Christ. The motherhood remains; the Son remains the center under God.",
